# `lib/` and `build/` above are Python packaging patterns, but they are
# unanchored, so they also match mobile/lib/ and mobile/build/ — the Flutter
# client's entire Dart source tree. Commit 92cc8e1 ("feat(mobile): add Flutter
# client") landed 92 files and 3683 lines of Android/iOS/Windows runner
# scaffolding with zero application code, because every .dart file under
# mobile/lib was silently ignored. A clone could not build the app.
#
# The directory itself has to be re-included before its contents can be: git
# will not descend into an excluded directory, so `!mobile/lib/**` alone does
# nothing. mobile/build/ stays ignored — that one is a real build artefact.
!mobile/lib/
!mobile/lib/**

